      "title": "Embeddings and the Vector Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Embeddings and the Vector Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What an Embedding Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Embedding== = fixed-length array of **floats** made by a model",
                "Typical sizes: {blue:384}, {blue:768}, {blue:1536} dims",
                "Similar meaning lands at ==nearby points=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Meaning Is Position",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pair",
                "Position"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "car / automobile",
                  "{green:close}"
                ],
                [
                  "car / banana",
                  "{red:far apart}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dimensions have ==no human-readable meaning==",
                "Only **distances and angles** between vectors mean anything",
                "Different models = different spaces and dims: ==never mix== them in one index"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Query and Chunking Rules",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Chunk",
                    "sub": "split long text",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Embed",
                    "sub": "one model",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Index",
                    "sub": "vectors",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Query",
                    "sub": "same model",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Rules",
              "items": [
                "Query and documents: ==same model==",
                "Models have a **token limit**: chunk first",
                "One vector over a long text blurs many topics"
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mixing models",
              "text": "Vectors from two models are **not comparable**, even when the dims match. A new model means ==re-embed everything==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Similarity Metrics: Cosine, Dot Product, Euclidean",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Similarity Metrics: Cosine, Dot Product, Euclidean",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Metrics",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Metric",
                "Formula",
                "Reading"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Cosine==",
                  "(a·b) / (|a||b|)",
                  "-1 to 1; angle only, ignores length"
                ],
                [
                  "==Dot product==",
                  "sum of a_i*b_i",
                  "fastest; higher = closer"
                ],
                [
                  "==Euclidean (L2)==",
                  "sqrt(sum (a_i-b_i)^2)",
                  "smaller = closer; sensitive to magnitude"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dot product ==equals cosine== when vectors are **L2-normalised** to length 1"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Worked Example",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import math",
                "def cos(x, y):",
                "    d = sum(i * j for i, j in zip(x, y))",
                "    return d / (math.hypot(*x) * math.hypot(*y))",
                "a, b, c = [1, 0], [1, 1], [0, 1]",
                "print(round(cos(a, b), 2), round(cos(a, c), 2))"
              ],
              "note": "a and b: 1 / (1 * 1.414)"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "0.71 0.0"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cosine ==0== means unrelated (right angle)",
                "Cosine near ==1== means same direction"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Using a metric **different** from the one the model was trained for",
                "Reading cosine ==distance== as if it were similarity"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Distance flips the direction",
              "text": "Cosine distance = `1 - cosine`. **Smaller** is closer, the opposite of similarity."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Vector Databases and Core Workflow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
